ana: opened PR to refresh SDK snippets for streaming + pagination + retries across Py/TS/Go. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4301. Goal: short runnable examples (8-12 lines), migration note (v1 next_cursor -> v2 resume_token), expected-output blocks. Please review.

ben: taking TS. Will add compact async-iterator + retry helper. Sketch: ```ts
async function* s(req){
  let t=0;
  while(t<3){
    try{ for await(const c of client.stream(req)) yield c; return }
    catch(e){ t++; await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,2**t*100)) }
  }
  throw new Error('fail')
}```
Pushing in a few.

carmen: Ill update Go to use a buffered channel + context cancel and show ResumeToken persistence. Compact snippet: ```go
ch:=make(chan string,8)
ctx,cancel:=context.WithTimeout(context.Background(),10*time.Second)
defer cancel()
go func(){defer close(ch);for r:=range client.Stream(ctx,req){select{case ch<-r.Token:case<-ctx.Done():return}}}()
for t:=range ch{fmt.Println(t)}```
Will note: persist ResumeToken after checkpoints.

